<ContentLayout
  title="About Stream Mix | Free Multistream Viewer"
  description="Learn why Stream Mix was built and how its free browser-based multistream viewer works with Twitch, YouTube, and Kick."
  heading="About Stream Mix"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix is a free browser tool for watching several live streams and
    chats in one customizable workspace. It was built for viewers who follow
    esports events, watch parties, co-streams, and creators broadcasting across
    Twitch, YouTube, and Kick.
  </p>

  <h2>One viewer for several platforms</h2>
  <p>
    Instead of arranging several browser windows, you can add streams from
    supported platforms to one grid. Each window can show video, chat, or both.
    Windows can be moved, resized, focused, and switched to compact-header mode.
  </p>

  <h2>Designed around local control</h2>
  <p>
    Stream Mix does not require an account. Your stream list, window positions,
    and display preferences are stored locally in your browser. The application
    embeds the official players and chat experiences supplied by each streaming
    platform.
  </p>

  <h2>An independent side project</h2>
  <p>
    Stream Mix is an independent open-source project. It is not affiliated with
    Twitch, YouTube, or Kick. Development focuses on practical multistream
    viewing, a flexible layout, and keeping the interface out of the way.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Build your stream layout</a></p>
</ContentLayout>
